Inspiration
-----------

Wanderer's Sketchbook (by JeanPierre)
  Scribe's task-pinning concept was inspired in part by Wanderer's Sketchbook.
  Credit and thanks to JeanPierre for the original mod.

Gearlock Firearms (by JeanPierre) — derived gear assets
  The Timer-tab gearworks' small/flanking gear geometry and texture are derived
  from JeanPierre's Gearlock Firearms mod (https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/60282),
  re-skinned to Scribe's palette. Gearlock's assets are licensed for reuse and
  modification; Scribe copies and modifies them and does not reference Gearlock at
  runtime. The large escape/great wheel is Scribe's own procedural generation, not a
  Gearlock asset. Thanks again to JeanPierre.

HarfBuzzFix (by Seralth) — independent Linux HarfBuzz crash fix
  Seralth independently diagnosed the same Linux/glibc HarfBuzz symbol-collision crash
  Scribe's own fix addresses, and shipped a standalone mod
  (https://mods.vintagestory.at/show/mod/66713, https://github.com/Seralth/harfbuzzfix)
  that isolates LibGUI's bundled native library via a Harmony patch on its loader. Scribe's
  own fix (src/Mod/ScribeHarfBuzzLoadFix.cs) independently reimplements that same technique
  from first-hand analysis of the shipped LibGUI DLL — his repository carries no license, so
  no source was copied — but the approach is his to credit. Thanks to Seralth for the
  corroborating diagnosis and a working, validated technique.
